From d32233cdd0048a01bda2f913434ca4d0be21b2a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 08:49:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: Add a verified PureSoft KeyMint TEE persona

Allow the PureSoft KeyMint implementation to expose a dedicated
TRUSTED_ENVIRONMENT persona for TEE Soft Emu Generate mode.

Add an explicit boot mode that can report a verified and locked boot
state without changing the behavior of the regular SOFTWARE KeyMint
device. Populate RootOfTrust with a usable verified boot key and hash,
using stable domain-separated fallbacks when the bootloader does not
provide a public key digest.

Also reject ASSOCIATED_DATA for operations that do not support AEAD
instead of silently accepting updateAad calls. Only AES-GCM operations
advertise AAD support, and rejected updates invalidate the operation
handle as required by KeyMint.

The existing factory entry point and default PureSoft behavior remain
unchanged.

Change-Id: I944aee1540532877ecf1685918c138e3b6add739
